            "color": "#0c0b0a",
            "align": "left",
            "weight": 400,
            "italic": false,
            "sp": 0,
            "text": "Time moves differently when stripped of urgency. Standing at the edge of the afternoon, watching light fold onto stone, one realizes how few things truly demand answering. Here, memory becomes geography.",
